          "short": "$y'=-\\dfrac{1}{(x+2)^2}$, $y''=\\dfrac{2}{(x+2)^3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x+2)^{-1}\\\\y'&=-(x+2)^{-2}\\\\y''&=2(x+2)^{-3}\\\\y''&=\\frac{2}{(x+2)^3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q1-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$y=\\dfrac{1}{(5x+4)^3}$",
